-- Sales channels and the sales points under them.
--
-- "vdmc" and "bo" are load-bearing rather than sample data, and are marked is_system so the
-- lifecycle operations refuse to archive or rename them. The "vdmc" code is a published
-- integration contract: the vending module names it by this string, so renaming it breaks every
-- kiosk already registered. "bo" carries the single sales point used when an order has no
-- physical selling place, which is what lets sales_point_id be NOT NULL.
--
-- Ids are fixed rather than generated and every insert is ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, so re-running
-- is a no-op - required for "vdmc" in particular.
--
-- Only vending points carry an external_reference_id, because only they were registered by
-- another module; the pair (channel, reference id) makes a retried registration resolve to the
-- point it already created. Human-created points carry none and there are many per channel, which
-- is why those uniqueness rules are partial_uniques_strict - the loose variant would also forbid a
-- second reference-less point per channel.


